### CI health, repository health and audit coverage

Three questions, three commands. **`bun run cat check:ci-health`** — do the
workflows pass, and are the Pages previews building
([`ci-health`](skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/ci-health.md); one workflow failed all 30
times over two months with nothing saying so, bean `xom7`). Do not "fix" a
dispatch-only workflow by dispatching it
([`memory/`](memory/two-workflows-fail-by-design-here-do-not-fix-them-by-dispatc.md)).
**`bun run cat health`** — the repository itself: how much of the publish branch
the previews occupy, what a clone costs, whether the work plan has duplicates or
unhonoured claims. Its checks are in `test/health/`, `health:list` names them,
and every threshold carries its **basis**. The same three rules as CI health
hold — could-not-determine is never clean, the tracking issue is edited in
place, and on `unknown` it is left untouched while the job fails — and **it
reports and never acts**: every finding's action is a person's
([`deletion-requires-confirmation`](skills/conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md),
bean `plj1`). **`bun run cat audit:coverage`** — what is audited at all, per
graph typology ([`audit-coverage`](skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md)).

### Actors, roles and skills — a role is a swimlane

> **An actor performs a task in a process as a role, using that role's skills.**

Nothing *is* a reviewer; somebody acts as one for the duration of a lane
([`role-model`](skills/process/process-core/role-model.md)). The audit is
`bun run cat kg:audit`.

### Subagents with persistent memory

`.claude/agents/` declares subagents with `memory: project`; each gets a
`MEMORY.md` of which the **first 200 lines** are injected. Entries are authored
as nodes under a declared `memory/` directory, and maintaining them is part of
the work ([`agent-memory`](skills/conduct/conduct-core/agent-memory.md)).

### Feature requests and CRDM

A feature request enters the CRDM requirements workflow rather than being
implemented directly ([`crdm-detect`](skills/sdlc/crdm/crdm-detect.md),
[`crdm-requirements-workflow`](skills/sdlc/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md),
[the methodology](docs/process/crdm-methodology.md)). **The process is
executable — do not hand-roll a phase tracker**: `workflow_start` /
`workflow_next` / `workflow_complete` run it, and `crdm_start` / `crdm_status`
should not be built. The interaction model as a whole is
[the agentic harness page](docs/concepts/agentic-harness.md).

### Say which process you are in, working an issue, and committing

- **Say which process you are in, every turn**, and when you switch — and the
  committed workflow instance is the evidence
  ([`process-state`](skills/process/workflow/process-state.md)).
- **Working an issue**: announce the branch when you create it, and re-check
  the issue for new *and edited* comments while you work
  ([`issue-working`](skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/issue-working.md)).
- **Commit early, commit often, always PR** (STRICT) — open the PR at the first
  commit, and do not hold a green PR back
  ([`continual-progress`](skills/sdlc/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md)). A folio
  may be stricter, and it wins.

